# React Native with Expo

React Native apps don't build with Vite. They use Metro, through Expo. The shared rules (TypeScript, components, state, testing) are the same as on web; this file covers what is different.

## Setup

- Use Expo (`npx create-expo-app@latest`) with the New Architecture and Hermes. Use a development build rather than Expo Go once you add native modules.
- Apply the team configs: `configs/tsconfig/tsconfig.native.json`, `configs/eslint/eslint.config.native.js`, Prettier.
- Config in `app.config.ts` (typed) rather than `app.json` when values come from env vars.
- Install native packages with `npx expo install` so versions match the SDK.
- Upgrade the Expo SDK at least once a year; run `npx expo-doctor` in CI.

## Navigation

- Use Expo Router (file-based) for new apps, or React Navigation if the project already uses it.
- Type route params. With Expo Router, enable typed routes.
- Each screen handles loading, error and empty states and has an error boundary (`ErrorBoundary` export in Expo Router).
- Validate params from deep links before use.

## Styling and layout

- Use `StyleSheet.create` or the project's styling library (for example NativeWind or Unistyles) consistently.
- Design tokens (colours, spacing, typography) live in one theme module. No inline magic numbers.
- Use Flexbox; avoid fixed widths and heights that break on small screens or large fonts.
- Respect safe areas with `react-native-safe-area-context`.
- Support light and dark mode with `useColorScheme`.
- Handle the keyboard on forms (`KeyboardAvoidingView` or `react-native-keyboard-controller`).

## Components

- Text must be inside `<Text>`. Guard conditional numbers (`count > 0 && …`) or the app crashes.
- Use `Pressable` for touchables, with `accessibilityRole`, a label, a pressed style and a 44×44 hit area.
- Use `expo-image` instead of `Image` for remote images.
- Platform-specific code: small differences with `Platform.select`; large ones in `.ios.tsx` / `.android.tsx` files with the same props interface.
- Share logic, hooks, types and API code with the web app; share UI only when it really fits both.

## Lists

- `FlatList` or `FlashList` for anything that can grow. Never `ScrollView` + `.map()` for long data.
- Stable `keyExtractor`, memoized row component, `renderItem` defined outside JSX.
- Provide `getItemLayout` (FlatList) or an `estimatedItemSize` where needed for smooth scrolling.

## Storage

| Data                            | Store                                    |
| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| Tokens, passwords, secrets      | `expo-secure-store`                      |
| Small non-sensitive preferences | MMKV or AsyncStorage                     |
| Larger structured offline data  | SQLite (`expo-sqlite`) or a sync library |
| Server cache                    | TanStack Query (optionally persisted)    |

Parse anything you read back from storage with a schema.

## Permissions and device APIs

- Ask for a permission only when the user starts the feature that needs it, and explain why first.
- Handle the denied and "don't ask again" cases with a path to Settings.
- Clean up subscriptions (location, sensors, `AppState`, `Keyboard`, `Linking`) in effect cleanups.

## Animations and gestures

- Use Reanimated and Gesture Handler so animations run on the UI thread.
- Respect reduced motion.

## Releases

- Build with EAS Build; separate `development`, `preview` and `production` profiles.
- Use EAS Update (OTA) only for JS changes; native changes need a store release. Use runtime versions to keep them compatible.
- Increment the version and build number on every store release.
- Test release builds on a real low-end Android device and an older iPhone before shipping.
- Crash and error reporting (for example Sentry) with source maps uploaded for each build and update.

## Testing

- Jest with the `jest-expo` preset and React Native Testing Library for components.
- Maestro (or Detox) for E2E flows on simulators and real devices.
- Use `testID` only where role or label queries aren't possible.
